KNOWNBUG
declaration_initializer_read1.sv

^\[main\.p0\] .*: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p1\] .*: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p2\] .*: PROVED .*$
^\[main\.p3\] .*: PROVED .*$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
All four are refuted. The initial blocks read the non-deterministic value
of the variable before the initial state, rather than the value of the
declaration initializer; --show-trans gives, e.g.,
main.n == nondet(main.n) + 1. Initial blocks that do not read the
variable, and always blocks, are not affected.
